<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani Fauji Fertilizer sags 3.71 pct.</title>
<headline>Pakistani Fauji Fertilizer sags 3.71 pct.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's blue-chip Fauji Fertilizer fell 2.35 rupees, or 3.71 percent, to 61 rupees on institutional selling early on Tuesday, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is heavy selling by a state-run institution in Fauji Fertilizer, as in other blue chips,&quot; dealer Sajjad Mankani of BMA Capital Management said.</p>
<p>&quot;Fundamentally it is a good scrip which has come under pressure because of the market's general weakness,&quot; said dealer Hina Akhlaq of KASB &amp; Co. Some 177,000 Fauji shares had changed hands in early trade.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
